Luvie @LUVIE_VERSION@

A pattern-based MIDI sequencer: https://github.com/benbriedis/luvie

This archive holds both halves of Luvie. Nothing here needs installing to run, but the
plug-in has to be in a place your host looks.

  bin\luvie.exe          the standalone application - run it from here if you like
  lib\lv2\luvie.lv2      the LV2 plug-in bundle
  LICENSES\              Apache-2.0, and the licences of the libraries built in


Installing the plug-in
----------------------

Copy the whole luvie.lv2 folder into your per-user LV2 directory:

    %APPDATA%\LV2\luvie.lv2

Create the LV2 folder if it is not there. Restart your host, or tell it to rescan, and
Luvie will appear among your plug-ins. Reaper, Ardour and Carla all read this location.


"Windows protected your PC"
---------------------------

Luvie is not code-signed yet, so SmartScreen warns about it the first time you run it.
Click "More info" and then "Run anyway". You will see the same warning whether you run the
.exe from this archive or use the installer -- signing is what removes it, not the choice
of download.

If you would rather not see it at all, install through Scoop instead:

    scoop bucket add luvie https://github.com/benbriedis/scoop-luvie
    scoop install luvie


MIDI and JACK
-------------

Luvie drives MIDI hardware and software instruments through the native Windows MIDI API
with no extra setup. JACK is optional: if it is installed, Luvie finds it at runtime and
offers JACK transport and JACK MIDI ports as well.
